.TH AVR\-ORG\-MEMBERS\-ACCESS 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-org-members-access \- Explain a member's effective access and where it comes from.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr org members access
[OPTIONS] MEMBER
.SH DESCRIPTION
Explain a member's effective access and where it comes from.
.PP
MEMBER is a user ID (usr-...), @me, an email address the member verified, or a display name that only one active member has. The answer lists the member's groups, what each grant reaches and why, and their organization capabilities. A partial answer says so.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr org members access @me
    avr org members access usr-0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef --json groups
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    governance, groups, notes, org_role, org_role_source, resource_access,
    resource_access_complete, resource_access_truncated, root_capabilities,
    user_id
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIMEMBER\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-org-members (1)
